                <pb facs="0982" n="970" sameAs="frus:frus1941v02/pg970"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War 1939/9393: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State to the Minister in
                        Yugoslavia</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Lane</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1941-03-28T18:00:00-05:00">March 28, 1941—6
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>58. Your 252, March 27, midnight. Since this Government has never withdrawn
                    recognition of the monarchy there is no special action required for recognition
                    of the new Cabinet under Premier Simović set up by King Peter. Therefore the
                    specific question raised in your telegram does not arise.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Welles</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
